@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+Root review: signed-transaction retry semantics (2026-10-23)
+Reviewed committed source 6ab298f196d93b60499178275acf025f5b8658af, profile-broadcast.js and actual test/site-wallet-profile-broadcast.test.mjs.
+The sendViaProfile loop CONTINUES to the next configured endpoint after transport/non-JSON failures and mismatched hashes. It sends exactly the same signed bytes. This is a legitimate idempotent propagation strategy; root is NOT requesting its removal or alleging double execution. The same transaction hash/nonce cannot execute twice on one canonical chain.
+However HANDOFF-S-F-WALLET-ROUTES.md says Unknown is not resent, the function doc says never resent here, and the final error says it is not resent. Those statements conflict with the actual loop. Explain that identical signed bytes may be retried across the configured profile, with no new signature/replacement/nonce, and that after exhausting endpoints an unknown outcome must be checked before creating another transaction. Preserve no public fallback and explicit owner selection.
+Existing drop-raw/refuse-raw test at lines173ff verifies unknown after actual inclusion but does not assert both origins saw identical bytes in this case. Add a focused assertion/coverage of that actual timeout recovery behavior when doing the next necessary affected test run; do not rerun unchanged broad suites for documentation alone. If you intentionally change retry policy instead, justify the availability tradeoff and align source, tests and handoff. No edits to your active tree by root.
